  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>rlocus</keyword>
  <short_description>Root locus of a SISO model.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>rlocus(sys)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>rlocus(sys, k)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>rlocus(sys1, sys2, ...)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[r, k] = rlocus(sys)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[r, k] = rlocus(sys, k)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>sys</param_name>
      <param_description>SISO dynamic system</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>k</param_name>
      <param_description>Vector of feedback gains</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>r</param_name>
      <param_description>Complex closed-loop pole locations, one column per gain</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>k</param_name>
      <param_description>Vector of gains used</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>The root locus function, <b>rlocus(sys)</b>, computes and plots the locus of the closed-loop poles of the feedback loop <b>feedback(k*sys, 1)</b>, that is the roots of <b>den + k*num</b>, as the gain <b>k</b> sweeps from 0 to infinity.</p>
    <p
    >Each branch starts at an open-loop pole (marked <b>x</b>) for <b>k = 0</b> and ends at a finite open-loop zero (marked <b>o</b>) or goes to infinity as <b>k</b> grows.</p>
    <p
    >When a gain vector <b>k</b> is supplied, those gains are used instead of the automatically selected range.</p>
    <p
    >With output arguments, <b>[r, k] = rlocus(sys)</b> returns the closed-loop pole locations and the gains without plotting.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="adv-cli"
      ><![CDATA[f = figure();
sys = tf([1 3], [1 3 2]);
rlocus(sys);
]]></example_item_data>
      <example_item_img
        src="../../images/rlocus_1.svg"
        align="middle"
        generate="true"
      />
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[G = tf(1, [1 3 2]);
[r, k] = rlocus(G);
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
